course: dictionary
lesson: 11120
title: Whiz: fast, clever, and whizzing about
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Whiz can name a person, describe how something moves, or mean mixing food in a blender. The context tells you which meaning to use. «She's a whiz at maths.» Here a whiz is a person who is very good at something.
explain: «A sledge at the top of a hill whizzes down with no push.» Whizzes is a verb here. Nobody is pushing the sledge, so it must be moving on its own, and it is moving very fast. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a sledge moves very fast down with no push" makes sense.
explain: In UK English, whizz can also mean to mix food quickly in a blender. «Whizz the soup until smooth» tells you what to do with the soup. It does not mean the soup should zoom around the kitchen! Always check which meaning fits the sentence around it.
fact: Whiz is a noun when it names a person who is very good at something, as in «a maths whiz».
fact: Whiz is a verb when it means to move very fast, often with a buzzing or whistling sound.
fact: A whiz can also be the buzzing or whistling sound that something makes as it goes past very fast.
fact: In UK English, the spelling is often whizz, and «whizz up» can mean to mix food quickly in a blender.
fact: Clue words help: «fast», «past» or «with no push» often mean whiz is about speed.
exercise: «Energy also hides in height: a sledge at the top of a hill whizzes down with no push.» What does whizzes mean here? | Climbs slowly up | *Moves very fast | Stays still at the top
exercise: «She's a whiz at maths.» What does whiz mean in this sentence? | A slow walker | A sound like a buzzing bee | A machine that mixes food | *A person who is very good at something
exercise: «So the canoe whizzes back into the Perak river.» Which word from the sentence tells you the canoe is moving fast? | river | into | paddles | *whizzes
test: «Whizz the soup until smooth.» In this sentence, what does whizz mean? | *Mix quickly in a blender | Throw the soup away | Stir slowly with a spoon | Heat it up in a pan
test: Priya's friend says, "Ask Priya, she's a whiz at spelling." What does whiz mean here? | A fast bike | Someone who is always late | A loud buzzing noise | *A person who is very good at something
exam: «The rocket will whiz past the Moon in seconds.» Which meaning fits best? | Mix quickly in a blender | *To move very fast | A person who is very clever | A quiet whisper
